\b Google Ads API — Design Document (Turquesa Agenda)\b0\par
\par
\b Company:\b0 Turquesa Agenda\par
\b Website:\b0 https://www.turquesaagenda.com.br\par
\b Contact:\b0 pedromusculini@gmail.com\par
\b Date:\b0 2026-08-26\par
\par
\b 1. Purpose\b0\par
Internal tooling to research keywords (Keyword Planner via KeywordPlanIdeaService), estimate CPC in Brazil (pt-BR), and optionally create/pause Search campaigns for Turquesa Agenda — a SaaS product for beauty salons in Brazil (scheduling, Google Calendar, WhatsApp wa.me links, billing).\par
\par
\b 2. Audience\b0\par
Internal users only (founder / operators). Not a public multi-tenant ads platform. No external clients will receive API access through this tool.\par
\par
\b 3. Architecture\b0\par
- Local Node.js scripts in the Turquesa Agenda repository.\par
- OAuth 2.0 Desktop client (Google Cloud) with scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords.\par
- Developer token from Google Ads manager account (MCC).\par
- Calls: customers:listAccessibleCustomers, KeywordPlanIdeaService.GenerateKeywordIdeas; later Search campaign setup in PAUSED state for review before spend.\par
\par
\b 4. Data handled\b0\par
- Google Ads account IDs, keyword ideas, search volume, competition, CPC estimates.\par
- No end-customer PII from salons is sent to the Ads API.\par
- Secrets stored only in local .env.local (not committed).\par
\par
\b 5. Compliance / safety\b0\par
- Campaigns created paused by default; human review before enable.\par
- Budget caps set manually in Google Ads UI.\par
- Intended use complies with Google Ads API Terms and Ads policies.\par
\par
\b 6. Access control\b0\par
Only authorized Google accounts under the company MCC can authorize OAuth. Token not shared with third-party agencies or resold tools.\par
\par
